      "q": 0.9799152773007701,
      "q_source": "stage2_saved_hidden_states[19]",
      "step_number": 3,
      "text": "Step 3: Use the properties of the rectangle to find the coordinates of \\(B\\) and \\(H\\).\n- Since \\(BE = 5\\) and \\(E\\) is at \\((6,3)\\), point \\(B\\) must be at \\((1,3)\\) because the vertical distance from \\(B\\) to \\(E\\) is 3 (same as the side of the square) and the horizontal distance is \\(5 - 3 = 2\\).",
      "z": 3.887506654839071
    },
