      "q_source": "stage2_saved_hidden_states[19]",
      "step_number": 4,
      "text": "Step 4: Find the coordinates of \\(H\\).\n- Since \\(H\\) lies on both the line through \\(B\\) and the line through \\(E\\) extended, we need to find the intersection of these lines with the line \\(AG\\).\n- The line through \\(B\\) and \\(E\\) has a slope of \\(\\frac{3-3}{6-1} = 0\\), meaning it is a horizontal line at \\(y = 3\\).\n- The line through \\(A\\) and \\(G\\) has a slope of \\(\\frac{3-0}{3-0} = 1\\), so its equation is \\(y = x\\).",
      "z": 0.34971275740550434
